course: dictionary
lesson: 11357
title: Zoo: a place and a busy noise
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A zoo is a place where wild animals are kept so that people can come and see them and learn about them. Good zoos also help rare animals by breeding them and keeping them safe.
explain: Words can have more than one meaning. «The classroom was a zoo» does not mean there were animals in the classroom. Try the meaning in the sentence: "The classroom was a very busy, noisy place" makes sense, so that is the meaning.
explain: When you meet a word you know, check whether it fits the sentence. The clues around the word show you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: A zoo is a place where wild animals are kept so people can see them and learn about them.
fact: Good zoos help rare animals by breeding them and keeping them safe.
fact: A zookeeper is a person who feeds and cares for the animals at a zoo.
fact: In speech, «a zoo» can mean a very busy, noisy place, as in «The classroom was a zoo».
exercise: What is a zoo? | A park with plants and no animals | *A place where wild animals are kept so people can see and learn about them | A shop that sells pets
exercise: «The classroom was a zoo.» What does zoo mean here? | *The room was very busy and noisy | There were lots of animals in the classroom | The class was going on a trip to the zoo
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means young birds: «Some rare birds lay a second egg if the first is taken, so a zoo can hatch two chicks instead of one.» | egg | rare | *chicks | second
test:
«A studbook records every animal of one kind in zoos: its parents, birth, moves and offspring.» What does a studbook record? | *Every animal of one kind in zoos, with its parents and births | Only the names of the zoo visitors | The price of tickets each day
Good zoos help rare animals. What is one way they help? | *By breeding them and keeping them safe | By selling them to pet shops | By letting them roam the streets
exam: «Singapore Zoo uses moats and plants instead of bars.» What does this tell you? | The zoo has no animals at all | The zoo only sells food | *The zoo keeps animals safe with water and plants rather than bars | The zoo is closed at night
